      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_266876adecac6cff9493c334ba691e315226d3c68c1cdf0684e909cacb99a5ef",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Batch evaluation and isolated evaluation optimize different costs: precomputation can amortize an FFT-style method over many Hardy-Z values without reducing the cost of one requested value, while processed-height-per-GHz-hour measures campaign throughput without normalizing sampling density, precision, or certification work.",
