    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_76091218e719bddeae5379df029cb59c7220eb68cdfe2195cc589e6ab708a0c1",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "A cheap computational policy should remain provisional when its ordering changes under the quantity that ultimately matters: Landau's score and the finite R0 calculation rank admissible polynomials differently, while Gram-block data show that an outer-first search order effective on common short blocks becomes inefficient on rare longer blocks. Downstream evaluation or observed conditional structure must therefore be allowed to rerank or branch.",
