    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_92945462294020a3ee218154ab22d111b3960855656463150fb9017f91bc02f2",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Both the static Lehmer-pair test and the heat-flow zero dynamics make a local gap configuration depend on the surrounding zeros: the former multiplies the gap scale by an all-other-zero reciprocal-square interaction, while the latter moves each real zero by a principal-value inverse-distance interaction. This is a structural comparison, not a derivation of either formula from the other.",
