      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Finite computation constrains the de Bruijn-Newman phase boundary through two opposite theorem-mediated interfaces: exhaustive RH verification beyond a stated height feeds a threshold theorem to give an upper bound for Lambda, while a certified exceptional pair feeds a pair theorem to give a lower bound.",
