      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_dbd8a036190bfd840143a953f6c70fec576f904f3e73e2aa586cd5aa45d87885",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Finite zero verification composes a lower count of critical-line witnesses with an independent exhaustive count for the same bounded region; equality leaves no room for additional off-line zeros. Because the comparison uses cardinality rather than refined ordinates, a later count-oriented implementation can discard unnecessary location detail after rigorously determining a sign change.",
